[TEXT] **Critical discovery in mswitch1's startup log:**

```
ip link set eth0.10 master br_vlan10  ← VLAN subs created first
ip link set eth4.10 master br_vlan10
...
ip link set eth0 master br_vlan1  ← physical ports enslaved AFTER
ip link set eth4 master br_vlan1
```

This ordering **enslaves eth0/eth4 to br_vlan1 AFTER the VLAN sub-interfaces were already created**. In Linux, once a physical interface is enslaved to a bridge, the bridge intercepts ALL frames — meaning eth0.10 and eth4.10 are **orphaned from real traffic** (br_vlan10 is isolated). Traffic IS flowing through br_vlan1.

